From d1c47cb0e5486915c4ce1e36b33f77545eb661e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jit Loon Lim <jit.loon.lim@altera.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:51:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(altera & intel): NJP support for ATF

Ciena NJP needs ATF SiP coverage for secure EFUSE/VAB mailbox
flows and a way to restrict which V3 SMCs non-secure world may
call. Without this, HPS cannot drive the required SDM commands
or enforce NS access policy for the NJP use case.

Refresh the ryo_optee ATF NJP patch against public altera-fpga
socfpga_v2.15.0 tip so it applies after the PSIRT default-deny
generic mailbox allowlist. Content matches innersource ATF #408
(NJP EFUSE/VAB SMCs + NS whitelist), with pubkey phase 2 at 0x28
and EFUSE_PUBKEY_PROGRAM payload helper macros.

Signed-off-by: Jit Loon Lim <jit.loon.lim@altera.com>
